From: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:55:13 +0000
Subject: feat(image): trace image view load events and painter state
 transitions

KuiklyPainter reaches State.Success only when the native image view has
fired both loadResolution and loadSuccess; until then the placeholder
stays. On HarmonyOS 1.13.0 11300010 a 720x1280 remote PNG is downloaded,
decoded and delivered by the cache pipeline (see the fetch trace) yet the
preview never leaves the placeholder, while a 300x200 JPEG does, and nothing
logged whether the ArkUI complete event arrived or which painter state the
events found.

OHOS KRImageView logs the adapter result kind (descriptor / newSrc /
error), every NODE_IMAGE_ON_COMPLETE with its loading status, picture size
and whether the success/resolution callbacks are registered, and
NODE_IMAGE_ON_ERROR. KuiklyPainter logs loadResolution / loadSuccess /
loadFailure with the state they found and every state transition. Ids are
url-free hashes; the two sides use different hash functions, so correlate
by time and src length.

Upstream-Status: pending
Fork-Patch: image-load-event-trace
Signed-off-by: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>

